                "reviews": [
                    {
                        "recommendationid": "36542453",
                        "author": {
                            "steamid": "76561198097035260",
                            "num_reviews": 259,
                            "playtime_forever": 19,
                            "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0,
                            "playtime_at_review": 19,
                            "last_played": 1511059392
                        },
                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Bought it for a multi-player games night. It's not just Pong/Arkanoid. There's a Move or Die style game rotation, so a single skilled player won't dominate every round. The graphics are dead simple, but there's no mistaking which paddle is yours. It can be appropriately frustrating at times with enough chaos to keep things balanced.\n\nTo the developer: please update the key bindings. A couple of the buttons are too easy to press during the game, which skips forward a round or exits to the menu.\n\nUpdate: after playing with friends, I have to change this review to a negative. The game modes were too frustrating to everyone -- too many different objectives. Some modes were frustrating and ended before the objective was evident, while others, like the maze levels, were annoying to complete. If you could remove certain levels from the playlist, that might solve the issue.",
